## The Real Kit We Stock: One ADJ Element H6 Pack, Six Wireless Fixtures

Uplighting, as a general term, means a fixture placed on the floor or low against a wall, aimed upward to wash that surface, a column or a piece of structure with color, rather than spotlighting a fixed point like a table or a couple. That is the general idea most searches for this keyword are after. What MEG actually stocks under that name is one specific product: an ADJ Element H6 Pack, a wireless, battery powered kit of 6 fixtures.

We are being precise here on purpose, because the honest answer to several of the questions this kit usually gets asked is "we have not confirmed that spec." Our equipment catalog does not list a battery runtime figure for this kit, so we are not going to invent one: our technician manages the fixtures through your event rather than promising a number of hours. We also have not confirmed an IP or weatherproof rating for it, so we do not market it as an outdoor fixture by spec, see [Outdoor Events](#outdoor-events-what-we-can-honestly-confirm-about-weather) below. And it does not carry a published DMX or app based color control feature: our technician sets the color for your event on site, it is not something you control yourself from a phone during the party.

<InlineCTA />

## Realistic Coverage: What 6 Uplights Can Actually Light

Most general guides to wedding or event uplighting assume a room needs somewhere between 12 and 24 units to wash an entire reception space in color. That is not what MEG's inventory supports, and we would rather say so directly than let you plan around a number our kit cannot deliver. Our real inventory is one kit of 6 fixtures.

What 6 fixtures realistically covers is accent lighting for 2 to 4 specific features of a venue, not a full room wash. In practice that means our technician places the kit against an entrance so guests walk into a lit threshold, along a head table or a ceremony backdrop to give it a colored edge, across a run of 2 to 3 columns in a venue with that kind of architecture, or on a single feature wall behind a stage or a dance floor. Tell us which feature of your venue you want lit when you book, and our technician will confirm what 6 fixtures can cover for that specific space, rather than assume a guest count formula that our real inventory does not back up.

## Uplighting or the Eco Pack's RGBW Spotlights: Which One Fits

MEG stocks two genuinely different colored lighting products, and mixing them up leads to the wrong booking. The uplighting kit is floor mounted, wireless and moved to wash a wall, a backdrop or a structure from below. The [Eco Pack's](/packages/eco/) RGBW LED spotlights are 2 light bars in a fixed position, set up and tested by our crew as part of that package, then run without a technician for the rest of the event.

| | Uplighting Kit | Eco Pack RGBW Spotlights |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Fixture count | 6, ADJ Element H6 Pack | 2 light bars |
| Placement | Floor mounted, wireless, positioned per venue feature | Fixed position, set up as part of the package |
| Effect | Washes a wall, backdrop or structure with color from below | Color changing accent light aimed as installed |
| Technician | Manages placement and color for the event | Delivered and tested, then self run |
| Included in a package | No, separate quote on request item | Yes, included in the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) |
| Price | No published a la carte price | 290 euros ex VAT (Eco Pack) |

Neither replaces the other. A dance floor that wants a fixed color changing accent, delivered and left to run itself, is what the Eco Pack's spotlights are for. A specific wall, backdrop or run of columns that needs washing in one steady color for the night is what the uplighting kit is for. If your event genuinely needs both, [contact us](/contact/) with your package and venue and we will confirm what is possible.

## Outdoor Events: What We Can Honestly Confirm About Weather

We have not confirmed a weatherproof or IP rating for the ADJ Element H6 Pack, so we do not market it as a rated outdoor fixture the way a spec sheet from a rental catalog might. What we can confirm is how our technician handles an outdoor booking in practice: they assess the conditions on site, place the kit around whatever shelter the venue genuinely offers, a covered terrace edge, an awning, a wall recessed from open sky, and recommend a covered backup position if rain is a real risk on your date. That is the same approach we take for our other outdoor setups, not a special exception invented for this page.

## Where This Gets Used: Weddings and Corporate MICE Events

**A wedding reception that wants a lit backdrop or a colored ceremony structure.** Our [lighting ideas for wedding rentals](/blog/lighting-ideas-for-wedding-rentals/) guide covers the Wedding Pack's fairy lights and the Eco Pack's RGBW spotlights in full, and names uplighting as the separate item that sits alongside both, not part of either package. If your reception wants one wall, a head table or a ceremony arch washed in color rather than the Wedding Pack's warm fairy light glow, this kit is the real option, quoted separately.

**A corporate keynote stage or a gala dance floor.** Our [event technology service](/blog/event-technology-service/) pillar already frames this kit as event lighting for "a keynote stage or a gala dance floor" alongside our compact LED light bar and Fresnel zoom wash light, for larger corporate stages rather than a small private party. A single feature wall behind a podium, or the columns flanking a stage at a MICE event, are exactly the kind of coverage 6 fixtures were built for. See our [AV technician hire](/blog/av-technician-hire/) guide for how the technician managing this kit fits into the rest of your event's technical crew.

## Pricing: A Separate, Quote Based Item

None of our four packages, [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/), [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/), [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) or [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), include the uplighting kit as a standard inclusion. Each package's own lighting, fairy lights on the Wedding Pack, RGBW spotlights on the Eco Pack, is covered in full on our [lighting ideas for wedding rentals](/blog/lighting-ideas-for-wedding-rentals/) guide. The uplighting kit sits outside every one of those package lines, the same way our [headset and lavalier microphones](/blog/headset-lavalier-microphone-rental/) have no published a la carte price. [Contact us](/contact/) with your package, venue and which feature you want lit, and we will confirm availability and a quote rather than make one up here.

